PATCH 232: reconstruct FUN_1000_55ae + thunk_FUN_1000_55ae (the STRSEG string-DRAW loop) -- a dropped
ES=STRSEG source base + the dropped char arg to the char-draw device method.  Asm-verified vs
re_out/fist_dat_image.bin 0x155a8-0x155c4.

Called by the viewport render (6686, patch 231) + others to draw a NUL-terminated STRSEG string one char
at a time via the FAR device method lcall [DGROUP:0x688].  Ghidra base-lost the source (`*param_1` host
deref of the raw si) and dropped the AL char arg to the draw call.  Rebased src = g_mem + (0x2d74<<4) + si
(ES is the hardcoded STRSEG 0x2d74); al threaded into the draw.  Both the entry thunk (0x155a8) and the
loop body (0x155ae) share this body.

Cascade-only => BEHAVIOUR-NEUTRAL for the 19 verify flows.  Default boot rc=0, mainmenu unchanged.  Sources
pristine; fist.c via build/.
